{"caveats":[],"characterization":[],"evidence":[{"char_end":436,"char_start":253,"chunk_id":"mdchk_4ac8744bc29f03a7","document_char_end":69673,"document_char_start":69490,"evidence_id":"ev_3aaedd397bd7f773","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"The DEMS measurements were conducted using a QAS 100 mass spectrometer with a detector (Linglu Instruments, Shanghai) to iden- tify the source of oxygen in the evolved gas during MOR.","source_sha256":"e8b42c47561c3fae960a6fabcefcd794e17c931fd4cb99e62cf05d8dc5b55f72"},{"char_end":600,"char_start":437,"chunk_id":"mdchk_4ac8744bc29f03a7","document_char_end":69837,"document_char_start":69674,"evidence_id":"ev_fe33583ca0f97f77","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"The catalyst ink was prepared by sonicating a mixture of 3 mg catalyst, 500 μL deionized water, 460 μLabsoluteethanol,and40μLof5wt%Nafion for 1.5 h in an ice bath.","source_sha256":"e8b42c47561c3fae960a6fabcefcd794e17c931fd4cb99e62cf05d8dc5b55f72"},{"char_end":880,"char_start":601,"chunk_id":"mdchk_4ac8744bc29f03a7","document_char_end":70117,"document_char_start":69838,"evidence_id":"ev_1d94e63c616f61c9","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"Before measurement, 30 μL of the well- dispersed ink was drop-coated onto a gold film electrodeposited on a polytetrafluoroethylene (PTFE) membrane (porosity ≥50%, aperture ≤20 nm, thickness ∼40 μm, Linglu, Shanghai) pre-labeled with 18 Oina 1 M KOH electrolyte containing H₂₁₈O.","source_sha256":"e8b42c47561c3fae960a6fabcefcd794e17c931fd4cb99e62cf05d8dc5b55f72"},{"char_end":748,"char_start":601,"chunk_id":"mdchk_4ac8744bc29f03a7","document_char_end":69985,"document_char_start":69838,"evidence_id":"ev_dd70e06ee99114a7","paper_id":"DOI:10.1038_s41467-024-50605-5","quote":"Before measurement, 30 μL of the well- dispersed ink was drop-coated onto a gold film electrodeposited on a polytetrafluoroethylene (PTFE) membrane","source_sha256":"e8b42c47561c3fae960a6fabcefcd794e17c931fd4cb99e62cf05d8